### D

1. With `type = "multiplicative"` we assumes that seasonality is proportional to the trend.
2. We used `stl(log(ts), ...)` because the original time series had an exponential trend.

### E




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
cbe <- read.table("../../sp26/rtp/data/cbe.dat", header = TRUE)
ts <- ts(cbe$elec,  start = c(1958, 1), frequency = 12)

ts.2 <- diff(ts, lag=1)
plot(ts.2)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](rtp02_exercise_03_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-5-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
cbe <- read.table("../../sp26/rtp/data/cbe.dat", header = TRUE)
ts <- ts(cbe$elec,  start = c(1958, 1), frequency = 12)

ts.3 <- diff(ts, lag=12)
plot(ts.3)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](rtp02_exercise_03_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-6-1.png){width=672}
